{#---
version: 1
changed_at: 2026-08-28
purpose: Detailed per-lead report -- an aggregate "leads summary" paragraph
         across everything one agent handled in a period, plus coaching-
         style feedback (what went well / what to improve). Same grounding
         data as the per-lead cards already shown in the report; this is a
         different synthesis over it, not a new extraction.
changes: v1 -- initial version.
---#}
You are writing two things for {{ agent.name }}'s daily performance report
at {{ agent.tenant.name if agent.tenant else "this property" }}: an aggregate
summary of every lead they handled today, and short coaching feedback.

THEIR LEADS TODAY
{% for l in leads %}
- {{ l.guest_name }} ({{ l.channel }}, status: {{ l.status }}){% if l.intent %}: {{ l.intent }}{% endif %}
  {%- if l.route_mentioned %} | route: {{ l.route_mentioned }}{% endif %}
  {%- if l.quoted_amount %} | quoted: {{ l.quoted_amount }}{% endif %}
  {%- if l.upsell_offered %} | upsell offered: {{ l.upsell_offered }}{% if l.upsell_accepted is not none %} ({{ "accepted" if l.upsell_accepted else "declined" }}){% endif %}{% endif %}
  {%- if l.ai_lead_analysis %}
  analysis: {{ l.ai_lead_analysis }}
  {%- endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% if not leads %}- No leads handled today.
{% endif %}

Respond with ONLY a JSON object (no markdown fences, no other text):

{
  "summary": "<2-4 sentences: an aggregate view across ALL the leads above -- what the day looked like as a whole (mix of outcomes, a common thread in what converted or stalled). This is NOT a repeat of any single lead's own analysis -- it's the pattern across all of them.>",
  "feedback": [
    {"type": "good", "text": "<one specific thing that went well today, citing a real lead/number above, or omit this entry if nothing stands out>"},
    {"type": "improve", "text": "<one specific, actionable thing to do differently, citing a real lead/number above, or omit this entry if nothing applies>"}
  ]
}

INSTRUCTIONS
- Ground every claim strictly in the leads listed above -- never invent a
  lead, outcome, or number that isn't there.
- "feedback" is coaching, not generic praise: name the specific lead or
  pattern that supports each item. If there's nothing genuinely worth
  flagging in one category, omit that feedback item entirely rather than
  manufacturing filler.
- At most 1 "good" and 1 "improve" entry -- pick the single most useful one
  of each, not a checklist.
- If there were no leads today, "summary" should say so plainly and
  "feedback" should be an empty array.
- Output only the JSON object.
